{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Threshold point first: the three artifacts describe one and the same trip, so the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08(a) is discharged and this case is triable rather than dismissible on identity. EV-TRIP-00529, EV-GPS-00529 and EV-FARE-00529 each carry trip_id TRP-00529; the trace's first fix opens at 2026-09-17T18:31:40+08:00, exactly the trip record's started_at, and its last fix at 18:55:40 precedes the fare ledger's charged_at of 18:56:00. The pickup and dropoff timestamps are consistent across all three, and no artifact's timestamps run backwards.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00529", "EV-GPS-00529", "EV-FARE-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trace is complete and is not impaired for policy purposes on any limb of POL-RD-07: it carries 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence over a 100% coverage window, with no gaps at all (max_gap_sec 0.0, gaps empty), no straight-line jump exceeding 500 m, and a sustained sampling interval far below 30 seconds. Because limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07 are not met, no POL-RD-07 consequence is triggered and there is no POL-GEN-02 discount to apply to any figure derived from this artifact: every derived number stands at its full weight of 1.0. That matters because POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement and expressly bars citation of the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold test — the platform's own trace, not a convenience copy, is the yardstick in this dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's answer to this dispute is that the clock ran because of traffic — 'meter waiting time is part of the fare, in every taxi in the world'. Nothing in the bundle supports that answer. The only traffic advisory in the pool, EV-ADVIS-00529-01, is MISSING: no payload, weight 0.0, and a BLOCKING MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code. I disclose that impairment expressly. POL-RD-03 exonerates only where an advisory names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, holds a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle reaching that segment, and is matched by a route that leaves the optimal corridor and rejoins it — no such advisory exists for the Orchard Turn to Kim Seng Promenade corridor in this window, and the driver's trace, whose derived.deviation.status is 'no deviation', shows no corridor departure and rejoin at all. The alternative exculpatory route is equally empty: EV-CHAT-00529 records message_count 0 with no messages, so no rider instruction exists for POL-RD-04 either. Under POL-RD-08 a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the driver's burden.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00529-01", "EV-TRIP-00529", "EV-GPS-00529", "EV-CHAT-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 5.40 the rider contests is not distance at all. It sits in the metered time and waiting lines of EV-FARE-00529: a time_charge of SGD 6.72 for 24.0 charged minutes against a platform optimal duration of 9.0 minutes, and a waiting_time_fee of SGD 3.08 against a recorded wait of only 1.0 minute on the trip record. Whether those time-based lines are properly chargeable turns on whether the delay was an external event — and the only artifact that could evidence that, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00529-01, is MISSING from this record at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. A traffic justification asserted against an advisory that is missing from the pool is precisely the POL-RD-10(5) situation, and if the tribunal's confidence on those lines cannot reach the platform floor of 0.70, POL-RD-10(1) points the same way. The rider accordingly asks for ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, so that under POL-GEN-03 the disputed amount is held rather than collected and a human reviewer can determine what, if anything, justified the time and waiting charges.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529", "EV-ADVIS-00529-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.waiting_time_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Candour requires one concession and it narrows the rider's ask rather than inflating it. Measured as POL-RD-01 requires — on the trace, which governs — the excess is 0.11 km and 4.400% of the 2.5 km optimal, so neither the 0.8 km absolute gate nor the 20% proportional gate is passed, no route deviation is established, and the POL-RD-02 recomputation has nothing to run on. The rider does not press a distance refund. Nor is any pass-through correction available under POL-RD-09: the fare carries zero ERP gantries, zero tolls and a zero airport surcharge, and nothing in the ledger is a phantom line for a gantry the trace never crosses. The rider's complaint is confined to the time and waiting charges and to the driver's unsupported explanation for them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00529", "EV-FARE-00529", "EV-TRIP-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on the rider's profile may be used against her, and the one profile field this category does allow is in her favour on its face: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the corroboration requirement that POL-RD-08 attaches to serial claimants is not triggered here and her account is not to be discounted on profile grounds. POL-GEN-01 confines every other field on either profile — rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation rate, prior counters — to context only, and the rider relies on none of them; the case must be decided on this trip's own trace, ledger and missing advisory.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00529"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

