    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties — this ruling concerns trip TRP-00529 (ION Orchard to Great World, 17 Sep 2026) and the SGD 5.40 the rider contests.\n\nROUTE DEVIATION — NOT ESTABLISHED. POL-RD-01 requires the excess over the booked optimal to exceed 20% of optimal AND 0.8 km in absolute terms, measured on the GPS trace, which governs over the trip record's rounded copy. The trace is clean: 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s. It measures the trip at 2.61 km against an optimal of 2.50 km — an excess of 0.11 km, or 4.400%. Both gates fail (4.400% < 20%; 0.11 km < 0.8 km), so no deviation exists and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The trip record's 2.60 km 'actual' is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and could not change that result.\n\nWHY THE TIME AND WAITING CHARGES STAND. The trip took 24.0 minutes against a platform optimal of 9.0 minutes, at recorded speeds of 4.6-8.2 km/h — a slow trip, consistent with the congestion the rider mentions. But fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED. The contested money sits in the metered time and waiting lines of EV-FARE-00529: time_fare SGD 6.72 for 24.0 charged minutes and waiting_time_fee SGD 3.08, within a charged_total of SGD 16.35. Under this policy the waiting-time fee is a properly chargeable component of a metered fare — POL-RD-02's own recomputation carries it — and the metered model charges for time spent in the vehicle. \"I didn't cause the traffic jam\" is not a ground for a refund under this policy. The POL-RD-02 figures on the ledger (recomputed_fare SGD 12.075, refund before rounding SGD 4.275) are conditional arithmetic computed on a deviation this trip does not establish, so nothing is payable from them. POL-RD-09 has nothing to refund either: no ERP gantries, no tolls, no airport surcharge, hence no billing-integrity defect.\n\nWHY THIS IS DECIDED, NOT ESCALATED. The rider asks for ESCALATE on the ground that the driver's explanation ('meter waiting time is part of the fare'; 'taxis charge for jams') needs a traffic advisory, and the only one in the pool, EV-ADVIS-00529-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. I do not escalate. POL-RD-10(5) fires when an exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact; no exculpatory clause was invoked here — the driver claimed no road closure and no route exoneration, and POL-RD-03 has nothing to exonerate because no deviation exists. The missing advisory is therefore noted (its absence is itself citable, and it carries no fact) but decides nothing. The other POL-RD-10 triggers do not fire: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c); trip identifiers and timestamps match across trip record, trace and ledger; there is no charge line without a counterpart; and the two sides' evidence is not in contradiction of comparable strength. POL-RD-10(1) does not bite, as the ruling rests entirely on artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0.\n\nNO REFERRAL. POL-RD-06 was consulted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 250 completed_trips_90d, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies, and no driver-conduct referral is produced. No other clause produces a referral. Both parties' profiles were used only as credibility context (POL-GEN-01); the rider's deviation_claims_60d is 0, so no additional corroboration was required of her.\n\nOUTCOME. NO_ACTION. The charge stands as billed (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00); nothing is refunded to the rider and nothing is paid to the driver. Confidence 0.95 — every artifact this ruling rests on carries weight 1.0, above the 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

