    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the outcome is NO_ACTION. The SGD 16.35 charged on EV-FARE-00529 stands; no refund and no driver payment issue, and no referral is added.\n\nRider — why your claim does not succeed. Your complaint is really about time lost in slow traffic, but the instrument that decides a route-deviation claim is the GPS trace, and it does not show a deviation. POL-RD-01 requires the driven distance to exceed the booked optimal by more than 20% AND by more than 0.8 km. The governing trace (EV-GPS-00529, complete, weight 1.0) measures 2.61 km against the booked optimal of 2.50 km on EV-TRIP-00529 — an excess of 0.11 km, or 4.4%. Neither gate is close. POL-RD-01 therefore directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised. The trace is not impaired (145 fixes at 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 s); its speeds of 4.6–8.2 kph show a slow crawl, not a detour, so this is a definite finding rather than an undecided one.\n\nConsequences. Because no deviation is established, POL-RD-02 never runs, and the conditional figures in the fare ledger (recomputed_fare 12.0750, refund before rounding 4.2750, payable 4.30) are arithmetic on a deviation this trip does not have; nothing is payable on them. The time_fare of 6.72 (24.0 metered minutes at 0.28/min) and the waiting_time_fee of 3.08 are the metered structure of a taxi journey, not a route deviation, and POL-RD-02 itself carries the waiting fee as a properly chargeable component. There is no billing-integrity correction either: the fare carries no ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge (erp_lines total 0.00), so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to refund.\n\nYour escalation request. I have considered it and it is not available. POL-RD-10(5) escalates where a party invokes an exculpatory clause against an artifact missing from the pool; the driver invoked no exoneration clause — his position is that the meter ran and that waiting time is part of every taxi fare — and there is no deviation for any such clause to excuse, so the absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00529-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) leaves no limb untested and changes nothing. That artifact can carry no fact, and a traffic characterisation does not become a ground of recovery merely because an advisory is absent. POL-RD-10(1) is also not met: the facts that decide this case rest on the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare ledger, all complete at weight 1.0, so confidence is well above the 0.70 floor.\n\nDriver. Your position is accepted. No deviation is established on the trace, the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 fails (and POL-RD-08 confirms a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by an advisory ID, shifts no burden), and you were never put to an exculpatory clause. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance (2.6 km) is not less than the trace distance (2.61 km), so POL-RD-04's compensation limb is not engaged.\n\nNeither profile decides anything. POL-GEN-01 confines both profiles to the tests that name their fields; the rider's deviation_claims_60d is 0, so no extra corroboration is required of her, and no context-only field (rating, account age, lifetime trips, or any prior counter) has been used against either party. Your record shows 0 deviation flags in 90 days across 250 completed trips, so POL-RD-06 establishes no pattern, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies, and no driver-conduct referral issues. The rider's account of a post-trip call is noted; no clause produces a referral for it on this record, because POL-RD-06(c) requires a repeat-deviation pattern your profile does not show. Confidence in this ruling is 0.90."
